  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking Tectoruside to SNU1 through a series of molecular interactions. Tectoruside is identified as a target for VMRC-LCP and Neridienone A, both of which are implicated in targeting SNU1. This implies that Tectoruside may act through a common intermediate, VMRC-LCP, which is a target of both compounds. The presence of a shared target (VMRC-LCP) and the sequential targeting of SNU1 by different compounds supports a possible mechanism involving the modulation of a shared biological pathway. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, suggesting that Tectoruside may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition or modulation of VMRC-LCP, which in turn affects SNU1. The integrated evidence highlights a plausible pathway where Tectoruside could influence SNU1 via a common target, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the role of VMRC-LCP in this process.",
